From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Wed Jun 3 00:00:00 2026
From: Carl Su <xuyusu@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Wed, 3 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] common: include stdint.h for SIZE_MAX

compat_overflow.c uses SIZE_MAX when GCC/Clang overflow builtins are not
available.  Some glibc toolchains, such as gcc-linaro 4.9.4 arm-linux-gnueabi,
do not expose SIZE_MAX from the currently included headers, so the fallback
implementation fails to build with:

  compat_overflow.c:44:61: error: 'SIZE_MAX' undeclared

Include stdint.h, which is the standard header that defines SIZE_MAX.

Signed-off-by: Carl Su <xuyusu@qti.qualcomm.com>
Upstream: Not submitted
---
 src/common/compat_overflow.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/src/common/compat_overflow.c b/src/common/compat_overflow.c
index d89212231..0a7d21731 100644
--- a/src/common/compat_overflow.c
+++ b/src/common/compat_overflow.c
@@ -27,6 +27,7 @@
 #ifndef HAVE_BUILTIN_OVERFLOW
 #include <limits.h>
 #include <stdbool.h>
+#include <stdint.h>
 #include <stddef.h>
 
 #define ADD_OVERFLOW(func, type, max) \
-- 
